.TH PREUPG-DIFF "1" "February 2017" "preupg-diff 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
preupg-diff \- manual page for preupg-diff 1.0
.SH DESCRIPTION
usage: preupg\-diff [\-h] [\-s] [\-v] [\-\-version]
.IP
analyzed_XML/folder [analyzed_XML/folder ...] new_XML
.PP
preupg\-diff compares multiple Preupgrade Assistant XML reports from which one
is new with unknown issues and the others have been already analyzed. The tool
helps to find new issues that emerged in the new report by filtering out those
results that are the same in the new report and at least in one of the
analyzed XMLs. The trimmed report is output in XML and HTML format and named
result_diff.xml/html.
.SS "positional arguments:"
.TP
analyzed_XML/folder
XML report with all issues already analyzed. Enter
either path to the XML or a directory, that contains
multiple XMLs. Possible to enter multiple XMLs \-
separate them by a whitespace.
.TP
new_XML
New XML report with possibly new issues
.SS "optional arguments:"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-simple\-html\fR
Generate simpler HTML than the default, without
clickable buttons, just long scrollable document.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print more detailedinformation about the processing.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The full documentation for
.B preupg-diff
is maintained as a Texinfo manual.  If the
.B info
and
.B preupg-diff
programs are properly installed at your site, the command
.IP
.B info preupg-diff
.PP
should give you access to the complete manual.
